    "result_text": "Done. Both new acceptance tests pass and the full build is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe requirement \u2014 default `registrationDate` to the server's current date when not supplied, and return it as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` \u2014 flows through the single `POST /api/owners` pipeline and back out via `GET`. I kept each piece in the layer where it belongs:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. This makes it a `LocalDate` on both `OwnerFieldsDto` (request) and, by inheritance, `OwnerDto` (response), and MapStruct maps it by name automatically \u2014 no mapper changes needed. Jackson serializes `LocalDate` as `YYYY-MM-DD`, matching the existing `Pet.birthDate` field.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `registrationDate` (`LocalDate`) entity field with `@Column(name = \"registration_date\")` plus getter/setter.\n\n3. **`DefaultRegistrationDate.java`** (new function step) \u2014 a small single-responsibility class: if the built owner has no registration date, set it to `LocalDate.now()`; a supplied date is left untouched.\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `applyRegistrationDate` step between `build` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance, following the project's function-injection convention rather than putting the logic into `BuildOwner`.\n\n5. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column so the mapped field persists. The test profile uses `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so that schema change is what makes the field round-trip; I updated all four for consistency.\n\nFull suite: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
